075.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135868075.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ray-of-hope-has-reached-gadchiroli-this-diwali-pm/articleshow/135868075.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ray-of-hope-has-reached-gadchiroli-this-diwali-pm/articleshow/135868075.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T04:29:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Choudhary and Mazhar Ali</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135868073,imgsize-1909162.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Those using Form 6 to re-enroll won't be prosecuted: EC to SC]]></title><description><![CDATA[The Election Commission has committed to include every eligible citizen in the electoral rolls during the current process. No legal action will be taken against individuals for re-registering to vote through Form 6. Voters are advised to ensure their names are not listed in other constituencies before applying. Additionally, those previously removed erroneously can submit fresh forms for their names to be reinstated.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/those-using-form-6-to-re-enroll-wont-be-prosecuted-ec-to-sc/articleshow/135867900.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/those-using-form-6-to-re-enroll-wont-be-prosecuted-ec-to-sc/articleshow/135867900.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T04:12:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dhananjay.Mahapatra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135867915,imgsize-240300.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No case against me anywhere,' he claims to TOI]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-case-against-me-anywhere-he-claims-to-toi/articleshow/135867879.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135867879.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Continued from P 1]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-case-against-me-anywhere-he-claims-to-toi/articleshow/135867879.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-case-against-me-anywhere-he-claims-to-toi/articleshow/135867879.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T04:06:25+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135867890,imgsize-68184.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lalit gets British citizenship, extradition prospects take a hit]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/lalit-gets-british-citizenship-extradition-prospects-take-a-hit/articleshow/135866282.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135866282.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Lalit Modi has announced his acquisition of British citizenship during an event at Oxford Union. While he claims to have faced threats and political persecution, he has refused to return to India. The Enforcement Directorate has ongoing investigations regarding his alleged financial misconduct linked to IPL. Previous requests for his deportation have been denied by the UK government.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/lalit-gets-british-citizenship-extradition-prospects-take-a-hit/articleshow/135866282.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/lalit-gets-british-citizenship-extradition-prospects-take-a-hit/articleshow/135866282.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T03:52:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Raj Shekhar Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135866278,imgsize-2369827.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Empty Vande Bharat allowed to run 463km despite 'poor power brake']]></title><description><![CDATA[An empty Vande Bharat train journeyed 463 kilometers from Hatia to Deen Dayal Upadhyaya station despite brake problems. Two loco pilots had reported issues with the power brake before the journey commenced. An investigation revealed that brakes on every coach had been isolated, leading to joint brake failure. The South Eastern Railway's document indicated staff negligence in integrating the braking systems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/empty-vande-bharat-allowed-to-run-463km-despite-poor-power-brake/articleshow/135865881.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/empty-vande-bharat-allowed-to-run-463km-despite-poor-power-brake/articleshow/135865881.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T03:23:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135865889,imgsize-189954.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Criminal killed in 5th 'encounter' in West Bengal since May]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/criminal-killed-in-5th-encounter-in-west-bengal-since-may/articleshow/135865864.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135865864.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/criminal-killed-in-5th-encounter-in-west-bengal-since-may/articleshow/135865864.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/criminal-killed-in-5th-encounter-in-west-bengal-since-may/articleshow/135865864.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T03:21:15+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.to